.TH CSTRING_SPLIT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_split \- split the string by a delimiter
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

cvec cstring_split(cstr s, const char *delimiter, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Splits s on every non-overlapping occurrence of delimiter and returns the
resulting tokens as a cvec of cstr (elem_size == sizeof(cstr)). Empty tokens
are preserved when the string begins or ends with the delimiter, or when two
consecutive delimiters appear. If delimiter is not found the vector contains
a single token equal to the original string.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s            String to split
delimiter    Separator string (must not be NULL or empty)
err          Optional pointer to receive an error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
cvec containing the tokens as individually heap-allocated cstr values
NULL on failure (details written to *err if err is non-NULL)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The caller is responsible for destroying every cstr inside the vector
as well as the vector itself:
  cvec parts = cstring_split(s, ",", NULL);
  for (size_t i = 0; i < cvector_elem_count(parts); i++) {
    cstr *p = (cstr *)cvector_at(parts, i);
    cstring_destroy(*p);
  }
  cvector_destroy(parts);
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_find (3),
.BR cstring_substring (3)
